   "start": 12.0,
   "end": 54.52,
   "text": "And then, about a month later, it was quite early in the morning, I think. She was in the kitchen, cooking, when she heard this amazing crash, and the whole flat shook. Really? It was the bedroom, yeah? Yeah, the bedroom ceiling fell down, on the bed. That's terrible. Was she okay? Yes, she was fine. She was in the kitchen. So what did she do? I can't really remember. I was so shocked when she told me, but I know she moved out of the flat. And that was your bedroom. Yes. It's a good thing you moved out when you did. Yes, that's what I thought. Anyway, when I moved into the next room.",
